{
	title: 'Terminal tool cards: status in the title, compact fold',
	spec: `Terminal tool cards spend rows on output, not plumbing.

Status in the title: a finished tool call shows its exit status and duration after the title, before the block link: "12:03 Description   (exit 1, 3.2s) #t4". The exit status shows only when nonzero; the \`[exit N]\` line no longer takes an output row (the model still receives it). Other bash status lines ("[timed out after 120s]", "[stopped by the user]", ...) stay in the output. Nonzero exit statuses use the warning colour (amber), never red, in the terminal and on the web; the web keeps the \`[exit N]\` line in its result text: a nonzero exit is often, but not reliably, a real failure. Duration shows when the call took 1 s or more, for every tool: with tenths under a minute ("3.2s", "50.2s"), then "1m 05s". While a call runs, its title shows elapsed time, "(12s)", updated every second from 1 s on. When the ticking row would scroll into scrollback, it is drawn without the time: a row there is never rewritten (that forces a canonical repaint, src/client/render.ts), and a stale time is worse than none; Ctrl-L shows it again. When a batch is drawn split (calls and results apart, frame.ts order), the status goes on the result block's header row. Background jobs do not tick.

The host stores each call's elapsed wall time in its tool_result block (\`ms\`), because a batch's results are written in one history record; older records have none and show no duration.

Fold: a closed result shows its first lines (itemView.resultRows). Leading and trailing blank lines are never displayed; a result with no visible output draws no result rows. Blank-line runs inside output stay as they are. When lines are hidden, the marker "… N more lines" goes at the right end of the last shown row if it fits with two spaces of gap, else on its own row.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Evidence from the 20 most recent sessions on the planning host (331 bash calls, 2026-10-05). Exit 1 is not reliably harmless: across all 4,386 bash calls on the host, 112 exited 1; 66 printed error text (No such file, fatal, usage), 13 printed nothing (grep/rg with no match). So all nonzero codes share one less alarming colour instead of exit 1 neutral and others red.',
		'Head or tail: of 275 folded bash results, 110 already end in | head, 47 are sed ranges and 18 rg; models pipe ./test through tail or grep themselves (32 calls). The first lines are the most informative, so the fold keeps the head.',
		'Blank lines: in those 366 calls, trimming changes 3 empty outputs and 5 leading blank lines; no folded view has trailing blanks or blank-line runs, so run-collapsing was not built (user decision: build only what changes real output).',
		"The host stores ms only when 1 s or more, so history records and exact-output test fixtures stay unchanged for fast calls. The running call reaches clients as optional call/since fields on the running state ('tools' phase), not a new event.",
		'Batch display order moved from frame.ts to src/client/batch-order.ts to keep frame.ts within the 400-line module limit.'
	],
	needs: ['1r'],
	foldInto: ['x1']
}
